{"duration_api_ms":26043,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"caab0429-5256-4399-a023-78987d1b0df4","total_cost_usd":0.92118,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97798,"cache_read_input_tokens":415900,"output_tokens":2780,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":847},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97798,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":208706,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65137},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2780,"cacheReadInputTokens":415900,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97798,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.92118,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":847,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I coded Juan Carrillo's one topic as rung 2, \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents,\" and wrote the label to `labels/coder-1.json`.\n\n**The evidence:**\n- **His vote:** he voted Aye on AB 1955 on 2024-06-27, in his current term. This was the Assembly's concurrence in Senate amendments (the bill's final Assembly passage). It passed 61-16, so 16 of 77 voted No. That is about 21%, above the 10% near-unanimous line.\n- **What the bill does:** the vote was on the chaptered text, not the earlier school-health version the Assembly passed on 2024-04-25. Section 220.5 forbids schools to \"enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches rung 2's only clause.\n\n**Why not the other rungs:**\n- **Rung 1:** Section 220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required to disclose\". It does not require them to keep anything from parents.\n- **Rungs 3–5:** the bill requires no notice to parents and no parental permission.\n\n**Two judgement calls a reviewer might read differently:**\n- **Preemption (V2):** the bill stops districts from requiring disclosure, which can look like the preemption pattern the codebook calls `adjacent`. I coded it `on-question` because rung 2 is itself about forbidding those rules.\n- **Single-subject (V4.1):** the bill also funds resources for LGBTQ pupils' families and bars retaliation against staff. I treated it as single-subject because every part concerns LGBTQ pupils' rights at school. A stricter reading would call it `multi-subject`, and a Yes vote would then show only direction.\n\nThere are no quotes, since the sources contain none of his own words, and nothing is listed as needing a source. The chair rests on one instrument, so it should get the `single-source` evidence tier.","ttft_ms":9268,"type":"result","duration_ms":27955,"uuid":"91df3c5e-1e25-41dc-a204-cbef659af3e6","ttft_stream_ms":1493,"time_to_request_ms":97,"first_content_frame_ms":1493,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
